  "question": {
    "text": "A bi-convex lens has radius of curvature of both the surfaces same as $1 / 6 \\mathrm{~cm}$. If this lens is required to be replaced by another convex lens having different radii of curvatures on both sides $\\left(R_1 \\neq R_2\\right)$, without any change in lens power then possible combination of $R_1$ and $R_2$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4bjBh",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3} \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $\\frac{1}{3} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wagAF",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5} \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $\\frac{1}{7} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jOPcu",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3} \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $\\frac{1}{7} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yWiod",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{6} \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $\\frac{1}{9} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "This will happen when<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_1}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_2} \\\\\n& (\\mu-1)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{-\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right)=(\\mu-1)\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}}\\right) \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}=\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}}<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
